WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
We cannot buy our security, our freedom from the threat of the bomb

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:11.000
by committing an immorality so great as saying to a billion human beings now

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:14.000
enslaved behind the Iron Curtain, "Give up your dreams of freedom,

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:19.000
because to save our own skins we're willing to make a deal with your slave masters."

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:23.000
Alexander Hamilton said, "A nation which can prefer disgrace to danger

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:26.000
is prepared for a master, and deserves one."

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:29.000
Now let's set the record straight.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:32.000
There's no argument over the choice between peace and war,

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:35.000
but there's only one guaranteed way you can have peace—

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:38.000
and you can have it in the next second: surrender.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:41.000
Admittedly there's a risk in any course we follow other than this,

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:46.000
but every lesson of history tells us that the greater risk lies in appeasement,

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:50.000
and this is the specter our well-meaning liberal friends refuse to face—

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:54.000
that their policy of accommodation is appeasement,

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:59.000
and it gives no choice between peace and war, only between fight or surrender.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:03.000
If we continue to accommodate, continue to back and retreat,

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:08.000
eventually we have to face the final demand: the ultimatum. And what then—

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:12.000
when Nikita Khrushchev has told his people he knows what our answer will be?

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:16.000
He has told them that we're retreating under the pressure of the Cold War,

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:20.000
and someday when the time comes to deliver the final ultimatum,

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:23.000
our surrender will be voluntary because by that time

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:27.000
we will have been weakened from within spiritually, morally, and economically.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:32.000
He believes this because from our side he's heard voices pleading for "peace at any price"

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:36.000
or "better Red than dead," or as one commentator put it,

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:38.000
he'd rather "live on his knees than die on his feet."

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:43.000
And therein lies the road to war, because those voices don't speak for the rest of us.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:47.000
You and I know and do not believe that life is so dear

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:51.000
and peace so sweet as to be purchased at the price of chains and slavery.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:55.000
If nothing in life is worth dying for, when did this begin—

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:59.000
just in the face of this enemy? Or should Moses have told the children of Israel

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:02.000
to live in slavery under the pharaohs?

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:04.000
Should Christ have refused the cross?

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:10.000
Should the patriots at Concord Bridge have thrown down their guns and refused to fire the shot heard 'round the world?

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:13.000
The martyrs of history were not fools,

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:19.000
and our honored dead who gave their lives to stop the advance of the Nazis didn't die in vain.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:22.000
Where, then, is the road to peace?

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:24.000
Well, it's a simple answer after all.

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:29.000
You and I have the courage to say to our enemies, "There is a price we will not pay."

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:33.000
"There is a point beyond which they must not advance."

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:38.000
And this—this is the meaning in the phrase of Barry Goldwater's "peace through strength."

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:43.000
Winston Churchill said, "The destiny of man is not measured by material computations.

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:47.000
When great forces are on the move in the world, we learn we're spirits—not animals."

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:52.000
And he said, "There's something going on in time and space, and beyond time and space,

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:55.000
which, whether we like it or not, spells duty."

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:58.000
You and I have a rendezvous with destiny.

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:02.000
We'll preserve for our children this, the last best hope of man on earth,

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:07.000
or we'll sentence them to take the last step into a thousand years of darkness.
